                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "439c2285-a325-3c2a-8c96-25a1a1bf6d48",
                                        "entry_id": "0483ce60-e822-327b-89a3-855d57c29863",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To secrete or store privately, as a hamster does with food in its cheek pouches."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d45e2842-8c0b-45c7-aaaf-f433a7368c31",
                                                "sense_id": "439c2285-a325-3c2a-8c96-25a1a1bf6d48",
                                                "text": "Probably the city government knew that without that hamstering half the city would starve and they somehow got the police to lay off. It was in the little stinky one-horse towns that you had all the trouble."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1007d13-5247-4186-8f13-0d0c592b8e4d",
                                                "sense_id": "439c2285-a325-3c2a-8c96-25a1a1bf6d48",
                                                "text": "[…] in his bedroom in neat stacks — he always hamstered them away upstairs as soon as the morning was done. This year the gifts sat ignored […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b19129b-8c62-4180-b7d2-4c206a240554",
                                                "sense_id": "439c2285-a325-3c2a-8c96-25a1a1bf6d48",
                                                "text": "[…] eastern children frequently “hamstered,” smuggled, and begged across the boundary, especially after currency reform […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
